			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4535115">
									

<p>The concept here is acceptable, and is introduced well. There are some areas where this could be cleaned up. For instance, the subject is designated -1, but we refer to only a specific instance (-2) in containment.</p>
<p>The interviews are fine, not my favorite dialogue. The issue for me was the ending. It kind of came out of nowhere, and just because the arms could move at superluminal speeds doesn't mean they themselves could as well. Also, you wouldn't really have a sonic boom moving at those speeds, you'd instead be dealing with [Cherenkov radiation <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherenkov_radiation">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherenkov_radiation</a>] (though you do hint at anomalous temporal effects).</p>
<p>But overall that detail at the end took me out of it. The overall execution was weak enough that overall, this is -1.</p>

